BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f1b0d3e3c6fe5ebd9fc86752
SUMMARY:Marsalis Premiere & Bruch's Violin Concerto
DTSTAMP:20260830T080329Z
DTSTART:20261002T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Performance Times October 2\, 2026 7:30PM Wynton Marsalis’ Libe
	rty promises a vivid musical portrait of America at 250\, told in the sing
	ular voice of a composer who uses the language of jazz to illuminate the n
	ation’s stories. A true documentarian of American history through sound\, 
	Marsalis brings a perspective that is both celebratory and clear-eyed\, we
	aving narrative and rhythm into a distinctly American tapestry. Nicola Ben
	edetti then gifts us a performance of Bruch’s beloved Violin Concerto\, wh
	ich grips the listener from its very first phrase and gathers momentum unt
	il the entire orchestra seems to glow from within. Urgent and emotional\, 
	the concerto lays its heart bare on the way to a fiery\, exhilarating fini
	sh. Program Max Bruch Violin Concerto No. 1 Wynton Marsalis Symphony No. 5
	\, Liberty (co-commission) Artists Cristian Mӑcelaru conductor Jazz at Lin
	coln Center with Wynton Marsalis Nicola Benedetti violin Info & Ordering M
	usic Hall Box Office 513-381-3300 1241 Elm Street | Cincinnati\, OH 45202 
	Located in the south entrance of Music Hall on Elm Street\; free 10-minute
	 parking is available in front of Music Hall. Additional Info and Hours\n\
	nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/marsalis-premiere-bruchs-vio
	lin-concerto
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/marsalis-premiere-bruchs-v
	iolin-concerto
LOCATION:Springer Auditorium\, Music Hall
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Classical Music
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
