BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:43a1d1eb8018410bdfac71fe
SUMMARY:Songs of Destiny
DTSTAMP:20260830T080329Z
DTSTART:20261017T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Performance Times October 17\, 2026 7:30PM October 18\, 2026 2:
	00PM From myth to fire to consolation\, this program traces a journey thro
	ugh passion\, virtuosity and reflection. Dorothy Howell’s Lamia opens with
	 a darkly lyrical\, evocative story of a nymph and her fate at the hands o
	f a jealous god. In her CSO debut\, violinist Alexandra Conunova brings fi
	ery energy and soaring lyricism to Khachaturian’s Violin Concerto\, one of
	 the 20th century’s great Romantic concertos. Two choral works by Brahms o
	ffer final consolation: Nänie laments the inevitability of death through t
	hree episodes from Greek mythology\, while Schicksalslied ("Song of Destin
	y") contrasts the eternal bliss of immortals with the restlessness of huma
	n existence. Program Dorothy Howell Lamia Aram Khachaturian Violin Concert
	o Johannes Brahms Nänie & Schicksalslied (“Song of Destiny”) Artists Crist
	ian Mӑcelaru conductor Alexandra Conunova violin May Festival Chorus\, Mat
	thew Swanson director Info & Ordering Music Hall Box Office 513-381-3300 1
	241 Elm Street | Cincinnati\, OH 45202 Located in the south entrance of Mu
	sic Hall on Elm Street\; free 10-minute parking is available in front of M
	usic Hall. Additional Info and Hours\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/eve
	nts/detail/cso-songs-of-destiny
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cso-songs-of-destiny
LOCATION:Springer Auditorium\, Music Hall
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Classical Music
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
