BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ef75dd869ad4bfdfa3eb74ac
SUMMARY:Gil Shaham Plays Tchaikovsky
DTSTAMP:20260830T080329Z
DTSTART:20261030T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:Performance Times October 30\, 2026 11:00AM October 31\, 2026 7
	:30PM Conductor Kwamé Ryan returns for a program of passion\, virtuosity a
	nd expansive Romantic expression. Legendary violinist Gil Shaham showcases
	 his expressive brilliance in Tchaikovsky’s Violin Concerto\, a perfect ex
	ample of the interplay between soloists and orchestra — at times in opposi
	tion to each other but always in sync. While 200 years apart\, Schubert’s 
	Ninth Symphony and Carlos Simon’s Fate Now Conquers are influenced by Beet
	hoven’s musical legacy (including some direct quotes!). Their individual s
	tatements attest to concepts of the Romantic — vast canvases of sound\, sw
	eeping melodies and heart-pounding climaxes. Program Carlos Simon Fate Now
	 Conquers Piotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky Violin Concerto Franz Schubert Symphony
	 No. 9\, The Great Artists Kwamé Ryan conductor Gil Shaham violin Info & O
	rdering Music Hall Box Office 513-381-3300 1241 Elm Street | Cincinnati\, 
	OH 45202 Located in the south entrance of Music Hall on Elm Street\; free 
	10-minute parking is available in front of Music Hall. Additional Info and
	 Hours\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cso-gil-shaham-play
	s-tchaikovsky
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cso-gil-shaham-plays-tchai
	kovsky
LOCATION:Springer Auditorium\, Music Hall
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Classical Music
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7a82c8c2c36d9474fa491c99
SUMMARY:Louis Langrée Conducts Ravel
DTSTAMP:20260830T080329Z
DTSTART:20261114T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:Performance Times November 13\, 2026 7:30PM November 14\, 2026 
	7:30PM The return of Music Director Laureate Louis Langrée brings us a foc
	us on Ravel’s music\, showing us the different styles in which Ravel compo
	sed throughout his life. His Ma mère l’oye is no better example of this\, 
	as the composer transports you through a fairytale of sound worlds\, each 
	offering an endless source of wonderment. In a similar exploration of musi
	cal styles\, the Tomasi Trumpet Concerto\, performed by Principal Trumpet 
	Anthony Limoncelli in his CSO solo debut\, brings together a full range of
	 colors and emotions. The program concludes with Ravel’s La Valse\, swirli
	ng with elegance before gradually unraveling\, and Boléro\, Ravel’s most w
	ell-known composition\, which grows from a single breath into a hypnotic b
	laze\, its unforgettable melody passing through every section of the Orche
	stra. Program Maurice Ravel Ma mère l’Oye (“Mother Goose”) Henri Tomasi Tr
	umpet Concerto Maurice Ravel La valse & Boléro Artists Louis Langrée condu
	ctor Anthony Limoncelli trumpet Info & Ordering Music Hall Box Office 513-
	381-3300 1241 Elm Street | Cincinnati\, OH 45202 Located in the south entr
	ance of Music Hall on Elm Street\; free 10-minute parking is available in 
	front of Music Hall. Additional Info and Hours\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiar
	ts.org/events/detail/cso-louis-langree-conducts-ravel
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cso-louis-langree-conducts
	-ravel
LOCATION:Springer Auditorium\, Music Hall
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Classical Music
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2a5f9364d6346c487c5b7577
SUMMARY:Strauss Spectacular
DTSTAMP:20260830T080329Z
DTSTART:20261122T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:Performance Times November 21\, 2026 7:30PM November 22\, 2026 
	2:00PM Conductor Phillipe Jordan\, in his highly-anticipated CSO debut\, l
	eads a Strauss spectacular for the senses. Also sprach Zarathustra opens w
	ith its world-famous sunrise\, sending a radiant surge of sound through Mu
	sic Hall. Death and Transfiguration\, written when the composer was merely
	 23 years old\, captures the essence of life and its beauty. At the end of
	 this life\, Strauss said\, “Death is as I composed it” referencing the mu
	sical motives used in this beautiful tone poem. At the heart of the evenin
	g\, the Oboe Concerto\, featuring CSO Principal Oboe Dwight Parry\, offers
	 pure\, elegant\, Mozart-like lyricism. Program Richard Strauss Tod und Ve
	rklärung (“Death and Transfiguration”) Oboe Concerto Also sprach Zarathust
	ra (“Thus Spake Zarathustra”) Artists Philippe Jordan conductor Dwight Par
	ry oboe Info & Ordering Music Hall Box Office 513-381-3300 1241 Elm Street
	 | Cincinnati\, OH 45202 Located in the south entrance of Music Hall on El
	m Street\; free 10-minute parking is available in front of Music Hall. Add
	itional Info and Hours\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cso
	-strauss-spectacular
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cso-strauss-spectacular
LOCATION:Springer Auditorium\, Music Hall
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Classical Music
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
