UID:dcb26b7738a8ebe9239f46cb
SUMMARY:Cristi Conducts Brahms Symphony No. 3
DTSTAMP:20260830T080329Z
DTSTART:20270109T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:Performance Times January 8\, 2027 7:30PM January 9\, 2027 7:30
	PM A chance discovery led to the revival of Florence Price’s music\, inclu
	ding her Ethiopia’s Shadow in America\, a full-bodied orchestral work whic
	h depicts the plight of Africans\, from enslavement to resignation\, faith
	 and adaptation. A new Cincinnati co-commission\, performed by Víkingur Ól
	afsson in its U.S. premiere\, Mark Simpson’s piano concerto is full of boi
	sterous rhythms and memorable tunes. The exploration of Brahms’ compositio
	ns continues under Music Director Cristian Măcelaru. Marked by moments of 
	conflict and instability\, introspection and clarity\, the Third Symphony 
	makes an argument for it being a truly autobiographical\, honest and profo
	und statement from the Viennese composer. Program Florence Price Ethiopia’
	s Shadow in America Mark Simpson Piano Concerto (US Premiere\; Co-commissi
	on) Johannes Brahms Symphony No. 3 Artists Cristian Mӑcelaru conductor Vík
	ingur Ólafsson piano Info & Ordering Music Hall Box Office 513-381-3300 12
	41 Elm Street | Cincinnati\, OH 45202 Located in the south entrance of Mus
