DESCRIPTION:Performance Times January 15\, 2027 7:30PM January 16\, 2027 7:
	30PM To tell the story of the American cultural tapestry\, we use love\, s
	pirituality\, innovation and diversity. Bernstein’s musical retelling of t
	he Romeo and Juliet story\, set in a modern-day American city\, is infused
	 with our human desire to find common ground despite tragic loss. Steven B
	anks refers to his own roots and spirituality in his composition Come As Y
	ou Are. The contemporary American sound\, defined by intricate rhythms and
	 innovative textures\, is heard in Jessie Montgomery’s Snapshots. Completi
	ng this beautiful American tapestry is none other than Duke Ellington\, wh
	ose style was defined by the elegance and sophistication he brought to the
	 swing and jazz genre. Program Jessie Montgomery Snapshots Steven Banks Co
	me As You Are Leonard Bernstein Symphonic Dances from West Side Story Duke
