	30PM Richard Strauss’ blends motifs depicting humor and heroism to reflect
	 Don Quixote’s quixotic adventures\, brought vividly to life by Alisa Weil
	erstein. CSO’s own Christian Colberg joins as the steadfast sidekick\, hel
	ping to tell this larger-than-life story. Enescu’s Symphony No. 3\, an ext
	raordinarily rare work not performed in America for at least a century\, w
	as written in the shadow of Dante’s Inferno. Scored for an orchestra of Ma
	hlerian proportions in size\, of Wagnerian power in scope and Bach-like te
	nderness in intimacy\, this composition offers a true universe of human ex
	istence — destiny\, transcendence and final peace. Our Music Director’s pa
	ssion for sharing Enescu’s genius makes him the ultimate interpreter of th
	is symphony. Program Richard Strauss Don Quixote George Enescu Symphony No
	. 3 Artists Cristian Mӑcelaru conductor Alisa Weilerstein cello Christian 
