DESCRIPTION:Performance Times Feburary 5\, 2027 11:00AM February 6\, 2027 7
	:30PM Tchaikovsky’s Romeo and Juliet\, aptly described by its composer as 
	a fantasy\, offers some of the most unforgettable love themes ever written
	. The journey from the passion of young love to its inevitable tragic end\
	, as written by Shakespeare\, has enthralled audiences ever since its prem
	iere. Bruckner’s Fourth Symphony\, known as the Romantic\, follows with ma
	jestic horn calls\, vast musical landscapes and towering symphonic archite
	cture that leaves the hall resonating with triumph. Program Piotr Ilyich T
	chaikovsky Romeo and Juliet Overture-Fantasie Anton Bruckner Symphony No. 
