UID:7189fa248f96bf2d52c36e52
SUMMARY:Extraordinary Women
DTSTAMP:20260830T080329Z
DTSTART:20270306T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:Performance Times March 5\, 2027 7:30PM March 6\, 2027 7:30PM C
	elebrate the extraordinary voices of women in music\, from pioneers of the
	 19th-century to trailblazers of today. Fanny Mendelssohn’s Overture in C 
	opens the program with elegance and poise\, followed by Emilie Mayer’s Fau
	st Overture\, whose dramatic flair showcases her command of orchestral col
	or. Clara Schumann’s Piano Concerto\, performed by the brilliant Alexandra
	 Dariescu in her CSO debut\, blends virtuosic brilliance with lyrical dept
	h. For much of the 19th century\, Clara’s musical presence inspired some o
	f the most important works by composers Johannes Brahms and her husband\, 
	Robert Schumann. The program culminates with music of today: Errollyn Wall
	en’s Concerto for Orchestra\, co-commissioned by the CSO. Selected by King
	 Charles III as Master of the King’s Music\, Wallen brings a distinctive\,
	 vibrant voice to the stage\, blending contemporary symphonic innovation w
	ith folk-inspired lyricism. Program Fanny Mendelssohn Overture in C Clara 
	Schumann Piano Concerto in A Minor Emilie Mayer Faust Overture Errollyn Wa
	llen Concerto for Orchestra (co-commission) Artists Cristian Mӑcelaru cond
	uctor Alexandra Dariescu piano Info & Ordering Music Hall Box Office 513-3
	81-3300 1241 Elm Street | Cincinnati\, OH 45202 Located in the south entra
	nce of Music Hall on Elm Street\; free 10-minute parking is available in f
	ront of Music Hall. Additional Info and Hours\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiart
	s.org/events/detail/extraordinary-women
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/extraordinary-women
LOCATION:Springer Auditorium\, Music Hall
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Classical Music
DURATION:PT2H
