	 Bach’s St. Matthew Passion is one of the most profound and moving works i
	n the choral repertoire. From the opening chorus to the final chorale\, Ba
	ch weaves a tapestry of human sorrow\, divine grace and ultimate redemptio
	n. The work’s intimate arias and powerful choruses illuminate the emotiona
	l depth of the Passion story\, moving seamlessly between movements of pers
	onal reflection and monumental spiritual drama. This is music that confron
	ts loss and suffering with honesty\, yet ultimately offers solace through 
	transcendence. Program Johann Sebastian Bach St. Matthew Passion Artists C
	ristian Mӑcelaru conductor Louise Alder soprano Karen Cargil mezzo-soprano
