BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:44b7508742e59a6d8ee39164
SUMMARY:Mozart & Prokofiev
DTSTAMP:20260830T080329Z
DTSTART:20270410T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Performance Times April 10\, 2027 7:30PM April 11\, 2027 2:00PM
	 It’s rare that two such in-demand artists make their CSO debuts on the sa
	me program\, one that takes the listener on a journey from spark\, to inti
	macy\, to ultimate triumph. Dobrinka Tabakova’s fanfare Orpheus’ Comet ope
	ns the program with a burst of energy\, its buzzing horn sounds passing th
	rough the Orchestra in a hypnotic loop. Pianist Isata Kanneh-Mason brings 
	us into a more reflective\, lyrical world with Mozart’s Piano Concerto No.
	 27. Prokofiev’s Fifth Symphony\, written in the final years of World War 
	II\, reveals perhaps the greatest melodist of the 20th century. His sympho
	ny is filled with both memorable tunes and sardonic humor\, culminating in
	 a chaotic whirlwind that hurtles the piece to an abrupt finale. Program D
	obrinka Tabakova Orpheus’ Comet Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart Piano Concerto No.
	 27 Sergei Prokofiev Symphony No. 5 Artists Delyana Lazarova conductor Isa
	ta Kanneh-Mason piano Info & Ordering Music Hall Box Office 513-381-3300 1
