DESCRIPTION:Performance Times May 14\, 2027 7:30PM May 15\, 2027 7:30PM Eac
	h of these three composers\, though it may not be evident at first\, made 
	significant contributions to diverse forms of musical entertainment. Eunik
	e Tanzil’s delicate\, pure and intimate work\, Remembering\, makes its muc
	h-anticipated Cincinnati premiere. Continuing in the same spirit of beauti
	ful\, cinematic music\, Korngold’s Violin Concerto — performed by supersta
	r Ray Chen — brings to life the Golden Age of the silver screen. Shostakov
	ich’s Tenth Symphony\, a deeply personal work\, reveals his conflict with 
	the Stalin regime and with the most human of expressions: love. This truly
	 autobiographical narrative portrays a steadfast rebel who criticizes whil
	e practicing quiet disobedience. Program Eunike Tanzil Remembering Erich K
